# In-copyright reference material — kept on disk, deliberately not tracked.
#
# reference/texts/additional/ holds private reference copies of works still under
# copyright (Campbell, Leiber, Bradbury, Jackson) plus the PDFs they were extracted
# from. Reading them locally is fine; committing them puts them in history, where a
# later `git push` would publish them and a rewrite would be needed to undo it.
#
# Harvey's "August Heat" in that folder IS public domain — move it to
# reference/texts/canon/ if you want it tracked.
reference/texts/additional/

# OS and editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Scratch
*.tmp
*.raw
scratch/

# Build products. Everything here is regenerated by render/build.sh.
render/out/
render/plates/
books/
__pycache__/

# Android app. The Capacitor project IS tracked — capacitor.config.json, the
# manifest, the theme, MainActivity and the gradle files are hand-edited and
# worth keeping. Everything below is fetched or generated by the build.
app/node_modules/
app/android/build/
app/android/app/build/
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/local.properties
app/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
app/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
*.apk

# The launcher icons and splash sheets under app/android/.../res/ ARE tracked,
# even though build_icons.py generates them: they are deterministic, small, and
# tracking them means a fresh clone builds an APK without a preliminary step.
